WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.792 --> 00:00:04.625
- I'm a city boy.

00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:05.471
I'm from New York.

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.560
I've never seen a cow
or anything like that.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.080
But hanging out with an emu is pretty cool.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.451
Probably won't have another opportunity

00:00:11.451 --> 00:00:14.284
like that for the rest of my life.

00:00:19.456 --> 00:00:23.680
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.931
(bird chirping)

00:00:25.931 --> 00:00:29.749
- We are at the Monroe County
Sheriff's Office Animal Farm

00:00:29.749 --> 00:00:32.160
on the grounds of the detention center.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.869
We have the capacity to have 700 inmates

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:38.411
in all three of our jail facilities.

00:00:38.411 --> 00:00:39.960
This is the main jail,

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.160
and we're the only facility of this kind

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.160
in the country that has
an exotic zoo at a jail.

00:00:47.309 --> 00:00:48.976
Ready for your corn?

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:54.456
It started out with just farm animals,

00:00:54.456 --> 00:00:58.920
and now I have exotic
animals of all varieties.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.989
Kinkajous are from the rainforest

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:02.699
of Central and South America.

00:01:02.699 --> 00:01:04.379
(bird chirping)

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:06.771
That's the bird we call
the I love you bird,

00:01:06.771 --> 00:01:09.429
and he is such a camera hog.

00:01:09.429 --> 00:01:11.371
We only take in animals
that have been abandoned,

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.451
abused, confiscated, or donated.

00:01:13.451 --> 00:01:14.851
Hi Tucker.

00:01:14.851 --> 00:01:16.979
We don't purchase any of the animals,

00:01:16.979 --> 00:01:18.490
and they're here for their life,

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.189
this is a forever home for them.

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:22.048
- I'm in here just for a year, you know,

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:24.419
and these guys are doing a life sentence.

00:01:24.419 --> 00:01:25.339
- Hi Moe.

00:01:25.339 --> 00:01:26.240
Alright Kramer.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.740
Did I wake you up pretty girl?

00:01:31.309 --> 00:01:33.476
Today I have four inmates.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:39.549
Every day they come down here
to feed, water, and clean

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:42.133
and then to spend time with the animals.

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:43.356
- What's going on buddy?

00:01:43.356 --> 00:01:44.960
You're going to get out pretty soon.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:46.536
Mandatory rec.

00:01:46.536 --> 00:01:49.085
- The farm is one of the
jobs in this facility

00:01:49.085 --> 00:01:50.845
that you can actually be outside all day

00:01:50.845 --> 00:01:52.564
and number two get to interact

00:01:52.564 --> 00:01:55.067
with a bunch of rare cool
animals like Kramer here.

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:57.538
He's got the little curl
on the top of his head.

00:01:57.538 --> 00:01:58.904
That's why we call him Kramer.

00:01:58.904 --> 00:02:00.168
- This is Eeyore.

00:02:00.168 --> 00:02:03.085
He was saved from a slaughter house,

00:02:04.447 --> 00:02:06.640
and he's a lot better off.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.097
- [Interviewer] Do you
think working with animals

00:02:08.097 --> 00:02:10.038
helps with their rehabilitation.

00:02:10.038 --> 00:02:12.697
- [Jeanne] I've seen a lot
of very positive changes.

00:02:12.697 --> 00:02:14.508
I've seen people that come down here

00:02:14.508 --> 00:02:16.278
and are completely scared of animals

00:02:16.278 --> 00:02:17.977
and by the end of their time here,

00:02:17.977 --> 00:02:19.975
many of them bring their families back

00:02:19.975 --> 00:02:21.628
to actually show them what they were doing

00:02:21.628 --> 00:02:23.518
when they were incarcerated.

00:02:23.518 --> 00:02:25.903
- I'm so happy to be out here.

00:02:25.903 --> 00:02:28.309
When I first came here,
he was like not even this big.

00:02:28.309 --> 00:02:30.968
Tiny and now look at you.

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:33.051
(laughs)

